  "sisId": "LEGL1501",
  "name": "Litigation I",
  "description": "Litigation is the process by which private disputes are resolved within the Alberta court system. This course examines the court structure and how to reference the Alberta Rules of Court. Students explore how plaintiffs bring claims to court and how defendants can defend against those claims. Introductory steps in a civil litigation dispute are covered up to a process called Questioning. Knowledge is applied by preparing key documents used in the civil litigation process.",
